    "narrative": "For today's matchup, the Zurich Zebras lean heavily on two middle-of-the-order power threats: **Junior Caminero** (80.95) and **Yordan Alvarez** (79.83). **Junior Caminero** draws a highly favorable assignment against Rodriguez, taking advantage of an elevated SP_xERA of 4.74, while **Yordan Alvarez**\u2019s elite 0.452 xwOBA makes him a set-and-forget option despite facing Kolek. In the outfield, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (63.38) and **Lars Nootbaar** (60.92) provide excellent value; **Pete Crow-Armstrong** benefits significantly from a dynamic platoon edge (+14%) and the premium leadoff spot, while **Lars Nootbaar** capitalizes on favorable wind and a strong platoon split against Bradley.\n\nRegarding roster management, **Chase Meidroth** (41.31) was the most difficult exclusion from the starting nine. While his score sits just above our baseline floor, the high quality of the opposition\u2019s arms\u2014specifically Sheehan\u2014pushed the optimizer to favor the higher offensive ceilings of **Luke Raley** and **Casey Schmitt** to maintain our competitive edge in the 5x5 categories. We continue to monitor the risk profile of **Gary Sanchez**, whose score of 42.46 is anchored by a challenging matchup against a sub-3.00 xERA pitcher in S\u00e1nchez. With **Hyeseong Kim** currently assigned to Oklahoma City and removed from our active calculation, our depth remains tested; we are relying on the steady output of **Trea Turner** (54.72) and **Kyle Schwarber** (55.33) to provide the stolen bases and power required to offset the potential drag of today\u2019s tougher SP matchups.",
